================================================================================
Algorithmic influences and attributions
================================================================================

Quadremesh is a clean-room managed-C# implementation. No third-party source code
is copied into it. The algorithms it implements are described in the following
works, and the permissively-licensed reference implementations below were
consulted for understanding only (and are built locally, never linked or
redistributed, solely as an offline test oracle — see
Agents/Docs/06-csharp-portability-analysis.md section 6.6).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Instant Field-Aligned Meshes (the core orientation/position field + extraction)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Wenzel Jakob, Marco Tarini, Daniele Panozzo, Olga Sorkine-Hornung.
  "Instant Field-Aligned Meshes." ACM Transactions on Graphics 34(6)
  (SIGGRAPH Asia 2015).
  Reference implementation "Instant Meshes": BSD-3-Clause.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
QuadriFlow (the pure-quad min-cost-flow extraction upgrade, P6)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Jingwei Huang, Yichao Zhou, Matthias Niessner, Jonathan Richard Shewchuk,
  Leonidas Guibas. "QuadriFlow: A Scalable and Robust Method for Quadrangulation."
  Computer Graphics Forum 37(5) (SGP 2018).
  Reference implementation "QuadriFlow": MIT License.

